            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Aaron L. Weisman, petitioner asks whether a sentence\u2011reduction motion filed before a conviction becomes final qualifies as an \u201capplication for post\u2011conviction or other collateral review\u201d under the federal statute."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f56255e24aa1d3ada1f16e94e2329e5ff669ed9cc7dd4ab3b1f9cc3c5f0c5aba",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f56255e24aa1-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "f56255e24aa1d3ada1f16e94e2329e5ff669ed9cc7dd4ab3b1f9cc3c5f0c5aba",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f56255e24aa1-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 8,
              "start": 8
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court is questioning how the phrase \u201cpost\u2011conviction or other collateral review\u201d should be interpreted, including whether it covers pre\u2011conviction motions."
      }
    ],
