            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Roberts, chief Justice Roberts opened the argument by announcing the case."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Aaron L. Weisman",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f56255e24aa1d3ada1f16e94e2329e5ff669ed9cc7dd4ab3b1f9cc3c5f0c5aba",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f56255e24aa1-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Aaron L. Weisman, weisman argued that the issue is whether the motion qualifies as an application for post\u2011conviction or other collateral review."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Aaron L. Weisman",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f56255e24aa1d3ada1f16e94e2329e5ff669ed9cc7dd4ab3b1f9cc3c5f0c5aba",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f56255e24aa1-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Aaron L. Weisman, weisman noted that such a motion can be filed within 120 days of sentencing or after affirmation on direct appeal."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f56255e24aa1d3ada1f16e94e2329e5ff669ed9cc7dd4ab3b1f9cc3c5f0c5aba",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f56255e24aa1-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Ginsburg asked whether the phrase includes post\u2011conviction or other collateral review and noted that a Rule\u202f35 motion is post\u2011conviction."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f56255e24aa1d3ada1f16e94e2329e5ff669ed9cc7dd4ab3b1f9cc3c5f0c5aba",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f56255e24aa1-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "f56255e24aa1d3ada1f16e94e2329e5ff669ed9cc7dd4ab3b1f9cc3c5f0c5aba",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f56255e24aa1-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor asked whether Rule\u202f35 would permit a federal challenge and whether the \u201cmagic words\u201d of an illegal sentence were \u201cillegal sentence\u201d or \u201cabuse of\u201d."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f56255e24aa1d3ada1f16e94e2329e5ff669ed9cc7dd4ab3b1f9cc3c5f0c5aba",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f56255e24aa1-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 8,
              "start": 8
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, justice Scalia expressed confusion about the phrase, suggesting it may include both post\u2011conviction and pre\u2011conviction collateral review."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "MR. WEISMAN",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f56255e24aa1d3ada1f16e94e2329e5ff669ed9cc7dd4ab3b1f9cc3c5f0c5aba",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f56255e24aa1-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 23
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "MR. WEISMAN argued that a Rule\u202f35 motion is not collateral review because it does not occur after the judgment becomes final."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Amicus brief",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f56255e24aa1d3ada1f16e94e2329e5ff669ed9cc7dd4ab3b1f9cc3c5f0c5aba",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f56255e24aa1-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 37,
              "start": 37
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Amicus brief, an amicus brief noted that judges often keep Rule\u202f35 motions pending for extended periods to retain the ability to modify the sentence later."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Ms. Mizner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f56255e24aa1d3ada1f16e94e2329e5ff669ed9cc7dd4ab3b1f9cc3c5f0c5aba",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f56255e24aa1-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 40,
              "start": 40
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "f56255e24aa1d3ada1f16e94e2329e5ff669ed9cc7dd4ab3b1f9cc3c5f0c5aba",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f56255e24aa1-0002-0008"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 52,
              "start": 52
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Ms. Mizner testified that a motion to correct an illegal sentence can be filed at any time and that a sentence becomes final when it is imposed."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f56255e24aa1d3ada1f16e94e2329e5ff669ed9cc7dd4ab3b1f9cc3c5f0c5aba",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f56255e24aa1-0002-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 44,
              "start": 44
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "f56255e24aa1d3ada1f16e94e2329e5ff669ed9cc7dd4ab3b1f9cc3c5f0c5aba",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f56255e24aa1-0002-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 45,
              "start": 45
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Alito raised a hypothetical about a sentencing judge exceeding the statutory maximum and asked whether a \u201ccollateral attack\u201d is defined as an attack on a judgment outside the proceeding that produced it."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f56255e24aa1d3ada1f16e94e2329e5ff669ed9cc7dd4ab3b1f9cc3c5f0c5aba",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f56255e24aa1-0002-0007"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 48,
              "start": 48
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kagan asked whether a petition for clemency presented to the governor would toll the limitations period."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f56255e24aa1d3ada1f16e94e2329e5ff669ed9cc7dd4ab3b1f9cc3c5f0c5aba",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f56255e24aa1-0002-0009"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 57,
              "start": 57
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, justice Sotomayor questioned how a Rhode Island court\u2019s limitation that challenges to an illegal sentence must be brought via Rule\u202f35 affects the finality of the conviction\u2019s affirmation."
      }
